<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103840" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηλουρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with distant boundaries</i>: hence, generally,
				<i>distant</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θονὸς πέδον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεδία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					889
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἶα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.543
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. οὖσα δωμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1325
				</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				4.360.38
			</span></i> (Pergam., <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>), and 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηλορός</span>
			.</div>
